00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:47.957
<i>Let me tell you a story about a young man called Oliver.</i>


00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:52.374
<i>There's no singing. No dancing.
And definitely no happy ending.</i>


00:00:53.205 --> 00:00:55.062
<i>But before we get to me,</i>


00:00:55.095 --> 00:00:57.399
<i>this all started with a thief
called Tom Chitling.</i>


00:01:06.134 --> 00:01:07.254
There he is!


00:01:07.287 --> 00:01:08.823
Stop! Stop!


00:01:27.031 --> 00:01:28.696
Let's go!


00:01:58.581 --> 00:02:00.919
- Come here! Where is it?
- I don't have it.


00:02:44.791 --> 00:02:47.383
<i>Growing up,
it was just me and Mum.</i>


00:02:47.414 --> 00:02:50.838
<i>We didn't have a lot,
but we had our imagination.</i>


00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.655
Where'd you take us
today, Oliver?


00:02:53.686 --> 00:02:56.566
The beach.
And we had an ice cream.


00:02:56.597 --> 00:02:58.359
Mmm, delicious.


00:02:59.318 --> 00:03:02.261
I took us
to the circus.


00:03:02.294 --> 00:03:04.951
Wow. Elephants.


00:03:04.982 --> 00:03:06.775
- Thanks, Mum.
- You're welcome.


00:03:06.805 --> 00:03:09.143
I'm gonna take us somewhere
even better tomorrow.


00:03:11.926 --> 00:03:13.527
I can't wait.


00:03:17.174 --> 00:03:18.807
What do you see?


00:03:18.837 --> 00:03:20.470
A lady swimming.


00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.358
What else?


00:03:23.255 --> 00:03:25.335
What does Oliver see?


00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:27.222
I don't understand,
Mum.


00:03:27.253 --> 00:03:31.798
Well, I see escape.


00:03:33.047 --> 00:03:35.703
I see a powerful woman


00:03:35.735 --> 00:03:37.783
leaving behind a life
that wasn't meant for her.


00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:42.551
And all of the flowers,
they're telling us why.


00:03:44.598 --> 00:03:48.214
Anyone ever told you
you're a bit weird, Mum?


00:03:48.886 --> 00:03:52.951
Has anyone ever told you
you're a bit cheeky?


00:03:52.981 --> 00:03:54.647
Shh!


00:03:54.679 --> 00:03:58.775
Oh. We're going
to space now, are we?


00:03:58.805 --> 00:03:59.862
Yeah.


00:04:01.078 --> 00:04:04.279
I thought we were supposed to be
doing our dreams for the future.


00:04:05.847 --> 00:04:07.511
I don't get it.


00:04:07.541 --> 00:04:10.358
Well that's you.
And that's me.


00:04:10.391 --> 00:04:12.311
And we're
in a gallery.


00:04:12.341 --> 00:04:16.022
And we're looking at this painting
of you and me in a gallery


00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.102
looking at this painting
of you and me in a gallery.


00:04:18.134 --> 00:04:20.119
And it goes on
and on and on...


00:04:20.919 --> 00:04:22.934
<i>But nothing
lasts forever.</i>


00:04:29.461 --> 00:04:31.189
<i>Then it was just me.</i>


00:04:31.222 --> 00:04:32.918
Poor lad.


00:04:34.966 --> 00:04:36.438
Time to go, Oliver.


00:04:36.469 --> 00:04:38.134
<i>I didn't know
anyone else.</i>


00:04:39.957 --> 00:04:41.814
<i>I certainly didn't belong
with them.</i>


00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.023
<i>I was better off on my own.</i>


00:04:58.006 --> 00:04:59.959
Oi! Wake up.


00:05:01.302 --> 00:05:03.126
Wake up,
you little rat.


00:05:03.158 --> 00:05:05.302
Right. I've told you before,
and I'm not... Hey!


00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:06.743
I'm not gonna
tell you again!


00:05:07.317 --> 00:05:08.823
Don't you dare.


00:05:08.855 --> 00:05:10.614
Sod off,
you little scrounger!


00:05:10.646 --> 00:05:13.047
Stop sleeping
in the gallery!


00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:15.702
<i>People don't really call
me Oliver any more. They call me...</i>


00:07:10.102 --> 00:07:13.270
Congratulations, love.


00:07:13.302 --> 00:07:14.710
You've won
a little yellow square.


00:07:14.741 --> 00:07:16.405
You could see
I had my hands full.


00:07:16.438 --> 00:07:17.814
They're not my rules.
I just enforce 'em.


00:07:17.846 --> 00:07:19.222
I was right here.


00:07:19.254 --> 00:07:20.566
You was right here
for too long.


00:07:20.598 --> 00:07:22.263
I thought
you were gonna move in.


00:07:22.294 --> 00:07:24.118
Do you think
I like doing this?


00:07:24.149 --> 00:07:26.486
Actually, I do.
It makes me feel big in every way.


00:07:26.518 --> 00:07:28.311
Could you not give
the ticket to anyone else?


00:07:28.342 --> 00:07:30.070
I'm not just giving 'em
to nice people.


00:07:30.101 --> 00:07:31.702
You look like a nice person,
so I've given one to you.


00:07:31.733 --> 00:07:33.558
Please, I was literally
about to leave.


00:07:33.589 --> 00:07:34.934
You should have left earlier,
shouldn't you?


00:07:34.965 --> 00:07:36.630
I can't afford this ticket.


00:07:36.662 --> 00:07:38.679
Well, I can't afford a 4K TV,
but I wish I could.


00:07:38.709 --> 00:07:40.278
I'd like one of those.


00:07:40.309 --> 00:07:42.166
Actually, I don't even know
what it is,


00:07:42.198 --> 00:07:44.278
but I like the sound of owning it.
I wish I could have it.


00:07:44.309 --> 00:07:46.133
- Please, sir...
- Please, please, please.


00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:47.894
Don't tell me
your problems.


00:07:47.925 --> 00:07:49.813
You're gonna get another one
in a minute. Oi!


00:07:49.845 --> 00:07:52.598
Hey, stay away from that van.
That's my van, you little pig.


00:08:03.254 --> 00:08:05.079
- Here you go, miss.
- Thank you.


00:08:13.109 --> 00:08:14.486
Stop that lad!


00:08:32.309 --> 00:08:34.454
Yo, man. The bikes!


00:08:47.797 --> 00:08:49.397
Yo, likkle man!


00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:52.182
Yo!


00:08:52.885 --> 00:08:54.775
- Hey, slow up, bro.
- What?


00:08:55.671 --> 00:08:59.094
Relax, man.
The cops packed it in way back.


00:08:59.125 --> 00:09:00.471
Why are you chasing me then?


00:09:00.502 --> 00:09:02.230
'Cause you forgot
your shopping.


00:09:05.013 --> 00:09:06.230
Okay.


00:09:11.573 --> 00:09:12.662
- It's you, isn't it?
- What?


00:09:12.693 --> 00:09:14.294
Doing all this.


00:09:14.902 --> 00:09:16.790
Come on, man,
we know that it's you.


00:09:16.821 --> 00:09:20.022
We done the forensics
on your spray cans.


00:09:20.053 --> 00:09:22.293
He's a joker, this one.
But, look, listen.


00:09:22.325 --> 00:09:24.245
I am Dodge,
this is Batesy,


00:09:24.277 --> 00:09:26.133
and together we...


00:09:33.078 --> 00:09:35.094
- What about your bikes?
- Not ours, pal!


00:09:42.677 --> 00:09:44.182
Come on!


00:09:47.317 --> 00:09:49.239
Hey! Stop!


00:09:54.293 --> 00:09:55.830
I said get down!


00:10:06.805 --> 00:10:09.302
Come on.


00:10:09.333 --> 00:10:11.541
- Cracking set of pins, love.
- Look at that.


00:10:11.573 --> 00:10:13.078
What happened to him?


00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:15.415
- What was that?
- Brilliant.


00:10:15.445 --> 00:10:17.078
You two again.


00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:19.702
Oh, come on.
We're your guardian angels.


00:10:19.734 --> 00:10:21.462
Where's the other guy?


00:10:21.494 --> 00:10:23.703
Come with us. We'll sort you out
with some new gear.


00:10:23.734 --> 00:10:26.454
Or you could just stay here.
I mean, it's up to you.


00:10:27.637 --> 00:10:29.206
We got trainers as well.


00:10:30.582 --> 00:10:32.118
Really?


00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:34.197
Come on, handsome.
Follow us.


00:10:38.742 --> 00:10:41.335
- I ain't got anything worth stealing.
- Come on, mate.


00:10:41.366 --> 00:10:43.990
You can't go through
life trusting no one.


00:10:44.022 --> 00:10:45.846
Yeah, we saved
your arse once already.


00:10:45.877 --> 00:10:47.542
That was
the other guy.


00:10:47.573 --> 00:10:49.493
What, you mean Red?


00:10:49.525 --> 00:10:51.383
Yeah.
The guy in the green jacket.


00:10:52.885 --> 00:10:55.030
That's a real hero,
that one.


00:11:04.214 --> 00:11:05.686
<i>Entre, s'il vous plaît.</i>


00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.357
<i>Who's that?</i>


00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.662
Just me and Batesy.


00:11:16.694 --> 00:11:18.263
What size waist are you?


00:11:18.294 --> 00:11:20.439
<i>I'd say he's about
a 30 regular.</i>


00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:22.166
Who's that?


00:11:22.196 --> 00:11:26.230
Oh, that is the ghost
of Dodge's grandpa.


00:11:26.262 --> 00:11:29.591
Batesy, shut up.
I'll introduce you later.


00:11:34.517 --> 00:11:36.341
Let's get you
some clobber first.


00:11:36.374 --> 00:11:38.006
Uh, you do realize
I've got no money?


00:11:38.038 --> 00:11:39.926
It's all right. You can owe us.


00:11:39.957 --> 00:11:41.718
I don't like
owing people.


00:11:44.309 --> 00:11:47.990
Go on, have 'em.
Introductory special offer.


00:11:48.405 --> 00:11:51.029
- We can spare 'em.
- Where did you get all this?


00:11:51.061 --> 00:11:53.942
- Sports Warehouse.
- Oh, I lost my favorite hat on that job.


00:11:53.973 --> 00:11:57.589
Are you ever gonna stop banging
on about that hat?


00:11:57.621 --> 00:11:59.542
- Huh?
- Probably not.


00:11:59.574 --> 00:12:03.605
Have 'em. They cost us nothing,
shop's claimed insurance.


00:12:03.638 --> 00:12:06.135
Plus, them pasty legs...


00:12:07.189 --> 00:12:09.141
they're gonna give me
nightmares.


00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:13.974
Oh, better give 'em a little bit
of a shake actually.


00:12:14.006 --> 00:12:16.279
Better give 'em
a shake first, eh.


00:12:21.173 --> 00:12:23.446
Hey, Fagin.


00:12:25.589 --> 00:12:28.470
Dodge, I've told you before.


00:12:28.502 --> 00:12:31.350
You cannot bring in green kids
off the street.


00:12:31.381 --> 00:12:33.525
- I know, but Fa...
- No buts.


00:12:33.557 --> 00:12:35.029
Out he goes.


00:12:35.061 --> 00:12:37.974
Fagin, please.
This is Twist.


00:12:38.454 --> 00:12:40.246
Extreme graffiti artist.


00:12:40.278 --> 00:12:41.910
Reaching places
others can't reach.


00:12:41.941 --> 00:12:43.862
Tags under moving cranes
and that.


00:12:43.894 --> 00:12:46.678
Like what's his face, uh...
Banksy. Yeah.


00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:49.431
Reaching places other people
can't reach, eh?


00:12:50.261 --> 00:12:53.622
The problem with graffiti is,
is you can't move it.


00:12:53.653 --> 00:12:56.343
What's the point in a painting
if it's always in the same place?


00:12:56.374 --> 00:12:59.254
The higher up I put my work,
the more people can see it.


00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:03.222
That's the point.
It doesn't belong to anybody.


00:13:03.253 --> 00:13:05.591
An idealist, eh?


00:13:05.621 --> 00:13:07.701
All property is theft.


00:13:08.341 --> 00:13:11.670
In my case,
that's literally true.


00:13:12.725 --> 00:13:15.317
Tell me, Mr. Idealist,


00:13:15.861 --> 00:13:18.166
how's virtue treating you?


00:13:18.198 --> 00:13:20.277
Is it filling your stomach?


00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:22.518
Can it give you
a hug on a cold night?


00:13:22.549 --> 00:13:25.878
Ideals are useless.
They're like appendix.


00:13:26.965 --> 00:13:28.213
Cut 'em out.


00:13:28.245 --> 00:13:29.365
He's fast.


00:13:29.398 --> 00:13:31.734
He left the Old Bill for dust.


00:13:31.765 --> 00:13:34.101
I thought maybe
we could train him up


00:13:34.134 --> 00:13:36.438
seeing as
we have a vacancy.


00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:37.877
I'm not a thief.


00:13:37.909 --> 00:13:40.822
What, you've never stole
a sarnie from Tescos?


00:13:40.853 --> 00:13:44.117
I don't need to. They chuck out
enough if you know where to look.


00:13:44.149 --> 00:13:46.229
Oh, living the dream.


00:13:46.261 --> 00:13:48.565
We all have to start somewhere,
don't we?


00:13:48.597 --> 00:13:51.446
It wasn't so long ago that you
were stealing credit card details.


00:13:51.478 --> 00:13:52.917
Uh, it's called phishing.


00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:55.093
It's called surviving.


00:13:55.126 --> 00:13:58.006
It's what we do
to survive.


00:13:58.933 --> 00:14:01.398
- Suppose.
- Bravo.


00:14:01.429 --> 00:14:02.774
You need a place to stay?


00:14:05.462 --> 00:14:06.614
No. Thank you.


00:14:07.446 --> 00:14:10.134
Cheers for the clothes.
I'll pay you back.


00:14:14.837 --> 00:14:17.077
That's
a really decent copy.


00:14:17.110 --> 00:14:19.926
I've seen the original tons
of times at the Tate.


00:14:19.956 --> 00:14:21.078
No, you haven't.


00:14:27.798 --> 00:14:30.262
I tell you what.
I'll cook tonight, Dodge.


00:14:30.293 --> 00:14:32.405
What do you want,
spaghetti or beef burgers?


00:14:32.436 --> 00:14:34.037
- I love the...
- Ah, nah.


00:14:34.069 --> 00:14:35.509
Come on. Do me a flavor, Fag.


00:14:35.541 --> 00:14:38.293
You know I'm 72% vegan.
Meat is a treat.


00:14:38.325 --> 00:14:41.685
Doesn't matter what you eat
so long as you eat together.


00:14:41.718 --> 00:14:44.886
Because, as I've always said,
the most important thing


00:14:44.917 --> 00:14:47.445
is the family
that eats together...


00:14:47.477 --> 00:14:49.397
...stays together.


00:14:49.429 --> 00:14:51.190
Yeah. Right.


00:15:00.021 --> 00:15:02.037
Oi! Mate.


00:15:02.996 --> 00:15:04.630
I just wanted to...


00:15:06.006 --> 00:15:07.510
Stand there gawping
like a fish?


00:15:08.245 --> 00:15:10.453
If you could speak sometime
soon that'd be great


00:15:10.484 --> 00:15:11.957
- 'cause I've got somewhere to go.
- I'm sorry.


00:15:11.988 --> 00:15:13.813
I didn't realize you,
you were a...


00:15:13.846 --> 00:15:15.413
And I didn't recognize you
with clothes on.


00:15:15.446 --> 00:15:16.885
I just wanted to say thanks.


00:15:16.917 --> 00:15:18.486
You're welcome.


00:15:19.605 --> 00:15:21.045
Is that everything?


00:15:22.646 --> 00:15:24.214
I'll take that as a yes.


00:16:51.476 --> 00:16:53.397
The boy's an artist.


00:16:53.429 --> 00:16:55.318
So, what do you see?


00:16:55.349 --> 00:16:58.005
A loner with a cracking pair
of trainers?


00:16:58.934 --> 00:17:01.366
Well, that's disappointing.
You missed the point.


00:17:04.021 --> 00:17:05.942
Can you get up there?


00:17:05.973 --> 00:17:07.957
Please. If he can...


00:17:08.598 --> 00:17:11.062
- Yeah.
- Some boys like respect.


00:17:11.893 --> 00:17:15.317
Some boys like being
in the pecking order.


00:17:15.349 --> 00:17:16.566
But this one...


00:17:17.174 --> 00:17:19.636
he wants something
that he's missing.


00:17:19.668 --> 00:17:21.110
A smartphone?


00:17:23.476 --> 00:17:24.917
He wants love.


00:17:24.949 --> 00:17:27.094
So let's give it
to him.


00:18:01.653 --> 00:18:03.734
Glad I climbed up
this side.


00:18:03.765 --> 00:18:04.853
Sorry!


00:18:04.886 --> 00:18:06.999
There's no toilet
up here.


00:18:07.478 --> 00:18:09.238
Love what you've done
with the place.


00:18:09.269 --> 00:18:11.478
It's just while
I'm doing this one here.


00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:15.733
Gonna offer me
a cup of tea then, or...


00:18:15.765 --> 00:18:18.166
I could do you cream crackers
and chocolate spread.


00:18:18.196 --> 00:18:19.830
Ooh, nutritious.


00:18:21.716 --> 00:18:23.637
I thought you were
a guy, by the way.


00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:25.494
That's why I was being
weird earlier.


00:18:25.524 --> 00:18:26.741
You say
the sweetest things.


00:18:26.772 --> 00:18:29.205
No, no. I wasn't...


00:18:29.238 --> 00:18:31.670
I mean, I just...


00:18:31.702 --> 00:18:35.125
- The way you move...
- Like a guy? Yeah. I get it.


00:18:35.862 --> 00:18:38.902
- I don't mean to offend you.
- Oh, why would that offend me?


00:18:38.933 --> 00:18:40.053
Just guys are more strong.


00:18:40.724 --> 00:18:42.549
Not that girls aren't strong.


00:18:42.582 --> 00:18:44.054
Girls are strong as well.


00:18:44.086 --> 00:18:45.974
Just guys tend to be...
I don't know.


00:18:46.006 --> 00:18:47.989
Not much of
a smooth talker, are we?


00:18:48.597 --> 00:18:50.358
Best stick to climbing
I think.


00:18:52.182 --> 00:18:53.814
How come you're so good
at climbing anyway?


00:18:57.396 --> 00:19:00.245
When I was younger,
I felt safer up high.


00:19:01.396 --> 00:19:02.998
People couldn't find me.


00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:06.901
So I taught myself
to climb.


00:19:07.381 --> 00:19:09.526
And you've been a loner
on a roof ever since?


00:19:10.196 --> 00:19:11.957
Suits me just fine.


00:19:13.301 --> 00:19:14.805
Well, you can't stay
up here forever.


00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:17.749
Isn't there things you wanna
see, things you wanna experience?


00:19:17.782 --> 00:19:19.414
Must get pretty boring.


00:19:19.445 --> 00:19:21.046
I can go anywhere I want.


00:19:22.549 --> 00:19:23.894
- What?
- See.


00:19:36.821 --> 00:19:38.262
I can imagine.


00:19:38.293 --> 00:19:41.301
Well, I'm here
in real life,


00:19:41.716 --> 00:19:44.405
and I've come to invite you
to a real-life dinner.


00:19:44.436 --> 00:19:46.005
Me and you?


00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:50.357
Come to Fagin's,
tonight at 7:00.


00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.853
And you never know,


00:19:52.885 --> 00:19:55.479
we might just be better
company than your paintings.


00:20:31.414 --> 00:20:32.694
What am I doing?


00:20:32.726 --> 00:20:34.389
What does Oliver see?


00:20:36.310 --> 00:20:37.302
Mum?


00:20:41.684 --> 00:20:43.093
Can't be by yourself forever.


00:20:48.341 --> 00:20:50.484
You're late.


00:20:50.516 --> 00:20:52.757
Is that any way to greet
your favorite supplier?


00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:58.133
What happened to Tom?


00:20:58.676 --> 00:21:00.533
He screwed up.
That's what happened.


00:21:01.366 --> 00:21:04.214
My kids are not disposable.


00:21:04.246 --> 00:21:06.806
That's exactly what they are,
my old friend.


00:21:07.541 --> 00:21:10.357
No friends, no family.
No questions.


00:21:18.164 --> 00:21:20.117
For complications.


00:21:26.452 --> 00:21:28.692
Did you get my envelope?


00:21:28.725 --> 00:21:30.230
What, this?


00:21:32.021 --> 00:21:33.654
When has it ever been
that easy, eh?


00:21:35.028 --> 00:21:36.468
I want in.


00:21:36.501 --> 00:21:38.389
I know you're pulling
a job.


00:21:38.421 --> 00:21:40.213
You're hitting Losberne.


00:21:40.692 --> 00:21:42.324
I want a cut.


00:21:42.357 --> 00:21:43.540
I was gonna tell you.


00:21:43.573 --> 00:21:44.726
Of course you were.


00:21:44.756 --> 00:21:46.485
Let me make it
easy for you.


00:21:46.517 --> 00:21:47.862
Whatever's in there...


00:21:48.949 --> 00:21:50.805
seems very important
to your little plan.


00:21:50.837 --> 00:21:53.077
Question is, are we gonna do it
the easy or the hard way?


00:22:02.805 --> 00:22:04.373
Partners.


00:22:11.285 --> 00:22:13.813
Partners. Now...


00:22:16.210 --> 00:22:16.629
the envelope.


00:22:17.652 --> 00:22:18.837
I think I'll keep it.


00:22:19.925 --> 00:22:22.358
Just in case
of future complications.


00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:41.974
Yeah.


00:22:42.004 --> 00:22:45.621
Took your bloody...
Oh, my giddy aunt.


00:22:45.653 --> 00:22:47.989
What is happening
with your barnet?


00:22:48.021 --> 00:22:50.485
Sorry.
Sorry, sorry, sorry.


00:22:50.516 --> 00:22:53.206
Come on, look, look.
Welcome, Twist.


00:22:53.237 --> 00:22:57.558
Let me take your jean shirt,
jacket for you. There we go.


00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:00.917
- Come on.
- Ah.


00:23:00.948 --> 00:23:02.772
Glad you could make it,
mate.


00:23:02.805 --> 00:23:05.269
Oh, Twist.
Come and sit next to me.


00:23:08.854 --> 00:23:11.957
Oh, blimey, look. Nancy,
take his beautiful flowers


00:23:11.989 --> 00:23:13.270
and put them in some water.


00:23:14.613 --> 00:23:15.733
Mmm.


00:23:18.389 --> 00:23:20.052
He can call me that.


00:23:20.085 --> 00:23:21.365
- You don't.
- Understood.


00:23:21.397 --> 00:23:24.821
I am starving.


00:23:24.853 --> 00:23:26.261
Dodge, please.


00:23:26.293 --> 00:23:28.022
Fagin, can we just
talk about something?


00:23:28.054 --> 00:23:30.230
Can we talk about our boy,
Batesy here,


00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:32.085
stealing my food
from under my bed?


00:23:32.116 --> 00:23:34.036
- Grass.
- Thief.


00:23:34.068 --> 00:23:36.694
- Okay, we're all thieves.
- Yeah, be a better one is the point.


00:23:36.724 --> 00:23:38.836
All right. Okay, okay.


00:23:38.869 --> 00:23:41.110
Uh, Twist,


00:23:41.141 --> 00:23:44.564
I want you to say a few words
because it's a tradition.


00:23:44.597 --> 00:23:47.126
About how thankful you are.


00:23:48.436 --> 00:23:52.117
Well, thanks for having me
round for dinner, I suppose.


00:23:52.149 --> 00:23:54.869
I can't remember the last time
that I sat down...


00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:56.566
Like a family?


00:23:57.589 --> 00:23:59.606
We're all orphans here.


00:24:05.301 --> 00:24:06.710
All right,
that's the thanks.


00:24:06.740 --> 00:24:08.373
Cool, um,
can we bloody eat now?


00:24:08.405 --> 00:24:10.454
- Yes! Eat. Eat.
- All right!


00:24:10.484 --> 00:24:12.404
- Eat.
- All right, all right.


00:24:12.437 --> 00:24:14.198
Let's go.


00:24:14.228 --> 00:24:15.702
Mmm.


00:24:23.925 --> 00:24:26.326
It appears that
you're a connoisseur of beauty.


00:24:26.997 --> 00:24:31.638
Yeah. I saw you in my office
admiring my collection, Mr. Twist.


00:24:32.725 --> 00:24:34.645
Can I stop using that name?


00:24:34.677 --> 00:24:37.013
It makes me sound
as though I'm in a casino.


00:24:38.004 --> 00:24:39.284
What else can I call you?


00:24:40.085 --> 00:24:41.108
Oliver.


00:24:41.140 --> 00:24:43.764
Oliver. Well, Oliver,


00:24:43.796 --> 00:24:46.100
your artwork is impressive.


00:24:46.133 --> 00:24:47.798
They're just copies.


00:24:47.829 --> 00:24:50.485
No, nothing is just a copy.
We always put a little bit


00:24:50.516 --> 00:24:52.533
of soul into everything,
don't you think?


00:24:53.749 --> 00:24:56.213
- Yeah, I suppose.
- When I was your age,


00:24:56.244 --> 00:24:58.293
I wanted to be an artist,
just like you.


00:24:58.773 --> 00:25:01.045
But my father was tasteless.
A bully.


00:25:01.076 --> 00:25:02.806
Oh, I'm sorry.


00:25:02.836 --> 00:25:05.685
Why sorry?
This is all my art, and Nancy...


00:25:06.868 --> 00:25:08.501
is my masterpiece.


00:25:08.917 --> 00:25:10.997
She needs someone to train with.


00:25:11.029 --> 00:25:13.301
Someone who can keep up
with her.


00:25:14.068 --> 00:25:18.228
- So you all just do whatever you want?
- Yes. But together.


00:25:18.261 --> 00:25:19.700
We never work alone.


00:25:19.732 --> 00:25:23.284
You know, we live together,
we eat together.


00:25:23.316 --> 00:25:25.044
Because the family
that eats together...


00:25:25.077 --> 00:25:26.932
Stays together. I know.


00:25:29.108 --> 00:25:30.197
Watch this,
watch this.


00:25:31.189 --> 00:25:33.014
Got a little surprise
for you.


00:25:33.044 --> 00:25:34.549
- For me?
- Yeah.


00:25:44.597 --> 00:25:45.909
Come on, then.


00:25:46.517 --> 00:25:48.853
You ready?
We're going out.


00:25:49.396 --> 00:25:50.998
Come on.


00:25:51.028 --> 00:25:53.877
Make sure you bring him back
in one piece.


00:26:04.277 --> 00:26:06.069
Don't you guys
ever feel bad?


00:26:06.645 --> 00:26:09.077
What? No.


00:26:09.109 --> 00:26:11.477
Look, the people that
we target are criminals anyway.


00:26:11.508 --> 00:26:14.198
So, it's justified,
innit?


00:26:14.228 --> 00:26:17.108
Think of Fagin
as good old Robin Hood


00:26:17.141 --> 00:26:18.773
and we're his Merry Men.


00:26:18.804 --> 00:26:20.053
Hmm.


00:26:46.741 --> 00:26:48.278
Oliver.


00:26:49.397 --> 00:26:50.644
Oliver.


00:26:50.677 --> 00:26:53.078
Hey, wake up. Come on.


00:26:54.485 --> 00:26:56.406
Get changed.
We're going out.


00:26:58.453 --> 00:26:59.893
Okay, give me a sec.


00:27:05.717 --> 00:27:08.214
- So, are you sticking around?
- Yeah, I think I will.


00:27:08.245 --> 00:27:10.069
You sure
you wanna do this?


00:27:10.101 --> 00:27:12.885
Yeah. It's nice
to belong to something.


00:27:13.749 --> 00:27:15.317
Trust me, you'll be fine.


00:27:28.821 --> 00:27:30.229
Morning, Dr. Losberne.


00:27:32.500 --> 00:27:33.685
Good morning.


00:27:37.589 --> 00:27:40.693
Dr. Crispin Losberne.


00:27:42.644 --> 00:27:44.661
Curator, art dealer


00:27:44.692 --> 00:27:48.244
and connoisseur
of 18th-century painters.


00:27:48.277 --> 00:27:50.805
He's very predictable,
which helps.


00:27:50.836 --> 00:27:56.053
Gets up every morning and leaves
for work at eight o'clock sharp.


00:27:56.085 --> 00:27:58.709
<i>He looks at his messages</i>


00:27:58.741 --> 00:28:02.645
<i>and he puts his phone away in the
right-hand pocket of his coat.</i>


00:28:02.676 --> 00:28:05.588
- Flat white.
- <i>Pays the barista.</i>


00:28:05.621 --> 00:28:07.445
Then he drinks his coffee.


00:28:07.477 --> 00:28:09.237
- Hmm.
- What's all this about?


00:28:09.268 --> 00:28:11.540
Well, we're gonna borrow
his phone.


00:28:11.572 --> 00:28:14.485
And have it back in his pocket
before he knows it's gone.


00:28:14.516 --> 00:28:15.956
But why?


00:28:15.989 --> 00:28:17.781
He took everything from me.


00:28:17.813 --> 00:28:18.997
Everything.


00:28:20.692 --> 00:28:23.476
And I'm going
to return the favor.


00:28:23.987 --> 00:28:27.253
First thing, we need
to hack Losberne's phone.


00:28:27.829 --> 00:28:30.133
Oh, and as far as the day
is concerned,


00:28:30.164 --> 00:28:31.604
it's all performance art.


00:28:31.637 --> 00:28:35.030
And the performance
will be given by Nancy.


00:28:37.428 --> 00:28:38.710
Oh!


00:28:38.740 --> 00:28:40.052
I am such a klutz.


00:28:40.085 --> 00:28:42.004
Let me help.
I've got tissues in my bag.


00:28:42.037 --> 00:28:43.510
You absolutely must
let me help.


00:28:43.541 --> 00:28:45.909
God, it's all over
your lovely jacket.


00:28:45.941 --> 00:28:47.350
Oh, I'm so stupid.


00:28:52.276 --> 00:28:53.780
I was on my way
to the Royal Academy


00:28:53.813 --> 00:28:55.285
to see
the Gainsborough exhibition.


00:28:55.316 --> 00:28:57.013
- Really.
- Oh, have you been?


00:28:59.605 --> 00:29:01.525
As a matter of fact,
I curated it.


00:29:01.556 --> 00:29:04.373
- Really?
- Oh, yes. Come on.


00:29:04.404 --> 00:29:06.614
- <i>Dodge, you got it yet?</i>
- Yeah, plugging in.


00:29:07.668 --> 00:29:10.964
All right.
On its way, Batesy.


00:29:10.996 --> 00:29:13.269
I'm quite a mover and shaker
in the art world.


00:29:13.300 --> 00:29:14.325
I have my own place.


00:29:14.357 --> 00:29:15.606
You have
your own gallery?


00:29:16.565 --> 00:29:18.228
<i>That working, Bates?</i>


00:29:18.260 --> 00:29:20.342
You don't ever need interns,
do you?


00:29:20.373 --> 00:29:21.492
Never say never.


00:29:23.221 --> 00:29:24.533
<i>Come on, Batesy.
Hurry up.</i>


00:29:24.564 --> 00:29:26.197
I'll give you my card.


00:29:26.229 --> 00:29:28.277
<i>I'm going as quick as I can.</i>


00:29:28.307 --> 00:29:29.589
It's in my jacket.


00:29:29.621 --> 00:29:30.773
Oh.


00:29:32.533 --> 00:29:34.069
<i>We need
to speed this up.</i>


00:29:34.101 --> 00:29:36.501
Yes, of course.


00:29:38.356 --> 00:29:39.765
- Oh.
- Bit wet.


00:29:39.796 --> 00:29:41.492
Hurry up,
hurry up, hurry up.


00:29:41.525 --> 00:29:43.125
Pop by anytime.


00:29:44.117 --> 00:29:46.838
- Goodbye.
- Dodge, quick, he's leaving.


00:29:51.220 --> 00:29:52.342
Quickly!


00:29:52.789 --> 00:29:54.262
Yes. Let's go.


00:30:01.044 --> 00:30:02.933
Garages on Swift Road.


00:30:12.437 --> 00:30:14.166
Someone's taken my phone.


00:30:28.468 --> 00:30:29.620
Get out of my taxi!


00:30:29.652 --> 00:30:31.702
Sorry, mate.
I thought it was free.


00:30:33.716 --> 00:30:35.444
- God.
- Is that what you're looking for?


00:30:37.269 --> 00:30:39.670
Yes. Thank you.


00:30:39.700 --> 00:30:42.068
You can keep the taxi.
I'm going to walk.


00:30:42.101 --> 00:30:43.893
Cheers.


00:30:46.997 --> 00:30:48.501
Where to, guv?


00:30:50.580 --> 00:30:52.245
Not bad for your first job,
Oliver.


00:30:52.276 --> 00:30:54.452
Yeah, and that was just
the hors d'oeuvre.


00:30:55.189 --> 00:30:58.196
Batesy, keep hacking.


00:30:58.229 --> 00:31:01.141
One word from Losberne,
I wanna hear it.


00:31:01.173 --> 00:31:03.734
We need to know his every move.


00:31:04.404 --> 00:31:05.908
- Dodge?
- Yeah?


00:31:05.941 --> 00:31:07.252
Do the washing up.


00:31:07.285 --> 00:31:09.461
Oh, man.


00:31:09.492 --> 00:31:11.764
Nancy, you're going
to art school.


00:31:11.796 --> 00:31:13.269
What?


00:31:13.300 --> 00:31:15.381
It's a crash course.


00:31:15.412 --> 00:31:17.748
If you're gonna be convincing
as an art student


00:31:17.781 --> 00:31:19.605
for an evening,
or even for ten minutes,


00:31:19.636 --> 00:31:22.036
you're gonna have to know
some art to talk about.


00:31:22.932 --> 00:31:24.916
Oliver, would you mind?


00:31:24.948 --> 00:31:26.773
- Of course.
- Ah, good.


00:31:27.222 --> 00:31:29.333
But nothing beats seeing
it in the flesh.


00:31:30.836 --> 00:31:32.757
This is about
Pope Nicholas.


00:31:33.493 --> 00:31:35.029
He's fuming.


00:31:35.061 --> 00:31:36.852
And Dante's... Shit.


00:31:37.525 --> 00:31:38.581
Wha...


00:31:38.964 --> 00:31:40.501
Guard.


00:31:41.300 --> 00:31:43.156
You do realize
this gallery's free, yeah?


00:31:43.188 --> 00:31:45.428
He's worked here
for years. He hates me.


00:31:45.460 --> 00:31:47.412
He's always throwing me out
for sleeping here.


00:31:48.852 --> 00:31:51.221
Get up.
Here, I got you.


00:31:52.757 --> 00:31:54.133
He doesn't scare me.


00:31:57.045 --> 00:31:58.581
Shall we...


00:32:08.276 --> 00:32:09.622
Millais's a genius.


00:32:10.582 --> 00:32:14.101
- The use of...
- Hardly gonna win the 500-meter backstroke, though, is she?


00:32:16.019 --> 00:32:17.750
I'm joking.
I know it's Ophelia.


00:32:18.900 --> 00:32:20.501
Anything else
you'd like to add?


00:32:22.067 --> 00:32:23.860
Well, personally,


00:32:23.891 --> 00:32:25.396
I think the flowers
in the painting


00:32:25.429 --> 00:32:27.317
are as important
as Ophelia herself.


00:32:27.828 --> 00:32:30.164
The floating flowers,
they represent her sorrow.


00:32:30.197 --> 00:32:32.437
And the nettles growing
around the willow,


00:32:32.468 --> 00:32:34.069
well that's...
that's her pain.


00:32:35.220 --> 00:32:36.949
Exactly.


00:32:36.980 --> 00:32:38.709
Did you do art
at school?


00:32:38.740 --> 00:32:41.844
No. It's just
common sense, innit?


00:32:41.876 --> 00:32:44.501
Well, that
and the Internet.


00:32:44.533 --> 00:32:46.741
All right.
Let's see what else you got.


00:32:56.020 --> 00:32:59.381
So, do you feel ready to be the most
convincing art student of all time?


00:32:59.412 --> 00:33:01.813
Yeah. Totally.


00:33:01.844 --> 00:33:03.924
Although no thanks
to my teacher. He was rubbish.


00:33:03.955 --> 00:33:05.268
Oi!


00:33:06.869 --> 00:33:08.022
So, uh...


00:33:09.172 --> 00:33:11.125
couldn't help
but notice old Ophelia


00:33:11.157 --> 00:33:12.885
made quite an impression
on you in there.


00:33:13.715 --> 00:33:15.254
Yeah.


00:33:16.372 --> 00:33:17.748
What was it about her?


00:33:21.428 --> 00:33:23.381
I used to go to
that gallery with my mum.


00:33:24.467 --> 00:33:25.812
She was an artist.


00:33:25.844 --> 00:33:28.276
Right.
That makes sense.


00:33:29.717 --> 00:33:31.989
- So, you did have a family?
- Just a mum.


00:33:33.204 --> 00:33:35.062
She wasn't around
for too long.


00:33:36.629 --> 00:33:38.357
Did you?


00:33:38.389 --> 00:33:39.860
Just a dad.


00:33:39.891 --> 00:33:41.588
But he was around
for too long.


00:33:44.627 --> 00:33:46.421
So why did you get
into free running then?


00:33:47.956 --> 00:33:49.206
So I could escape.


00:33:50.004 --> 00:33:51.349
Escape from what?


00:33:53.620 --> 00:33:55.508
From boys called
Oliver Twist.


00:34:01.076 --> 00:34:02.516
Come here!


00:34:03.700 --> 00:34:08.213
<i>To pull this job off, we'll
need the plans for Losberne's gallery.</i>


00:34:09.460 --> 00:34:11.380
<i>Oh, not
the caterpillar tash.</i>


00:34:11.411 --> 00:34:12.980
- Hello.
- Good morning, sir.


00:34:13.013 --> 00:34:14.741
We spoke on the telephone


00:34:14.773 --> 00:34:17.717
about your conversion
of number 30.


00:34:17.748 --> 00:34:19.188
The Losberne Gallery?


00:34:19.221 --> 00:34:21.877
I have bought
the building opposite


00:34:21.909 --> 00:34:25.844
and I want you to make it modern
like number 30.


00:34:25.876 --> 00:34:28.756
I have the plans here. I can show
you what we did for Dr. Losberne.


00:34:28.787 --> 00:34:30.420
Follow me.


00:34:32.981 --> 00:34:35.828
Yes. Very nice,
very nice.


00:34:38.868 --> 00:34:39.861
<i>Da.</i>


00:34:39.892 --> 00:34:42.804
11:05 on the dot, Fagin.


00:34:42.835 --> 00:34:44.468
Just like you said.


00:34:55.605 --> 00:34:57.493
This is private.


00:34:57.525 --> 00:35:00.021
It's okay.
I don't understand Russian, so...


00:35:01.525 --> 00:35:03.125
You want my business?


00:35:04.052 --> 00:35:06.549
Certainly.
Take your time.


00:35:06.580 --> 00:35:07.988
Thank you.


00:35:18.101 --> 00:35:21.173
No windows, reinforced walls.


00:35:22.164 --> 00:35:23.157
That's the one.


00:35:23.731 --> 00:35:25.844
That'll be
a job getting in.


00:35:25.876 --> 00:35:27.381
We don't have to do that.


00:35:27.924 --> 00:35:30.644
If we do
what I've got planned,


00:35:31.125 --> 00:35:32.693
they bring it out.


00:35:32.724 --> 00:35:34.036
Batesy, carry on.


00:35:34.067 --> 00:35:35.445
Bring what out?


00:35:36.021 --> 00:35:39.604
This is the painting
we're gonna steal.


00:35:39.636 --> 00:35:42.773
One of six paintings
by William Hogarth.


00:35:42.805 --> 00:35:45.493
That says Dotheboy's
Auction House, Fagin.


00:35:45.524 --> 00:35:47.060
Why are we casing up Losberne?


00:35:47.093 --> 00:35:48.885
The painting
was lost in a fire,


00:35:48.917 --> 00:35:51.828
but many people believed
it was a cover-up for a theft.


00:35:51.860 --> 00:35:55.029
All this time,
it's been off the radar.


00:35:55.060 --> 00:35:57.781
So you're saying
Losberne's got it?


00:35:57.813 --> 00:35:59.892
- He's the seller.
- Wait, hang about.


00:35:59.924 --> 00:36:01.460
How did he get his hands on it?


00:36:01.492 --> 00:36:04.533
Many years ago,
Losberne went into partnership


00:36:04.564 --> 00:36:06.612
with a man called
Isaac Solomon.


00:36:06.644 --> 00:36:09.044
Both of them bought
a lot of paintings.


00:36:09.076 --> 00:36:11.444
One of them was the Hogarth.


00:36:11.475 --> 00:36:13.299
But when they had it in auction,


00:36:13.331 --> 00:36:17.044
Losberne went missing
with the paintings.


00:36:17.075 --> 00:36:19.540
- Oh.
- And Solomon had nothing,


00:36:19.572 --> 00:36:22.740
and his credibility
as an art dealer was gone.


00:36:23.220 --> 00:36:26.773
Later, Losberne said
the paintings had been stolen.


00:36:26.805 --> 00:36:28.180
So my man tells me.


00:36:29.044 --> 00:36:31.605
How long have you been there?
I didn't hear you come in.


00:36:31.636 --> 00:36:33.236
You should be more careful,
Fagin.


00:36:33.268 --> 00:36:34.996
You're getting sloppy
in your old age.


00:36:38.900 --> 00:36:40.373
Oh,
it's only you two.


00:36:40.405 --> 00:36:43.829
Oliver, there's someone
I'd like you to meet.


00:36:45.587 --> 00:36:46.580
Oliver.


00:36:49.045 --> 00:36:50.325
Here, boy.


00:36:50.805 --> 00:36:52.564
This is Bullseye.


00:36:52.596 --> 00:36:53.652
Aw...


00:36:54.131 --> 00:36:56.372
You're gonna need
your hands later.


00:36:58.195 --> 00:36:59.828
Round two.


00:37:02.292 --> 00:37:03.829
Magnetic, see?


00:37:04.244 --> 00:37:06.004
Stick it on a pipe and get out.


00:37:16.596 --> 00:37:18.356
Oh, I'm so sorry.
Is it a bad time?


00:37:19.604 --> 00:37:21.012
It's the perfect time.


00:37:31.155 --> 00:37:32.884
Thank you.


00:37:33.843 --> 00:37:34.836
Bottoms up.


00:37:34.869 --> 00:37:36.277
Oh.


00:37:37.012 --> 00:37:38.421
Cheers.


00:37:44.147 --> 00:37:46.067
So, you were saying
it'd be answering the phones,


00:37:46.099 --> 00:37:47.891
doing a little bit of filing?


00:37:47.923 --> 00:37:50.260
Nothing a girl
like you couldn't handle.


00:37:50.837 --> 00:37:53.557
I did actually want
to show you some of my art.


00:37:54.292 --> 00:37:55.733
Street art, you say?


00:37:55.764 --> 00:37:57.557
Yeah,
it's just on here.


00:38:01.397 --> 00:38:02.932
<i>Let me just find them.</i>


00:38:03.604 --> 00:38:05.173
<i>Uh, yes. Okay.</i>


00:38:05.780 --> 00:38:07.125
This one is actually
based on...


00:38:07.156 --> 00:38:09.044
William Blake.
Of course.


00:38:11.156 --> 00:38:13.268
I love what you've done
with the line there.


00:38:14.420 --> 00:38:16.692
<i>These are actually
rather intriguing.</i>


00:38:16.724 --> 00:38:17.780
<i>Don't gas me.</i>


00:38:19.220 --> 00:38:20.756
Come on, girl.


00:38:20.787 --> 00:38:21.973
Give her a second.


00:38:22.004 --> 00:38:23.924
Sorry,
that's my graffiti talk.


00:38:23.956 --> 00:38:26.229
It's the only way to get taken
seriously on the street.


00:38:27.603 --> 00:38:29.237
Oh, right.


00:38:29.267 --> 00:38:31.061
Well, don't forget
your wine.


00:38:31.092 --> 00:38:33.107
Do you know, it's just going
straight through me.


00:38:33.139 --> 00:38:35.060
I must pop to
the little girls' room.


00:38:41.268 --> 00:38:42.741
Is it downstairs, or...


00:38:43.732 --> 00:38:45.012
Straight down
the stairs.


00:38:45.044 --> 00:38:46.516
The door straight
in front of you.


00:38:48.723 --> 00:38:50.612
Okay. Thanks.


00:39:06.068 --> 00:39:08.788
Oh, no. No, no, no.
He's on the move.


00:39:17.236 --> 00:39:19.988
- <i>I could have blown my hand off.</i>
- Yeah, calm down.


00:39:20.021 --> 00:39:22.260
- Everything all right?
- Yes, I'll be up in a minute.


00:39:22.293 --> 00:39:24.117
You better have brought
a spare.


00:39:24.148 --> 00:39:25.141
Uh...


00:39:29.109 --> 00:39:30.837
We just gotta get it
to her.


00:39:30.868 --> 00:39:31.893
I'll take it.


00:39:32.276 --> 00:39:33.717
I'm the climber,
right?


00:39:33.747 --> 00:39:36.020
Whatever you do,
don't drop it.


00:40:08.468 --> 00:40:10.356
Red, it's me.
Let me in.


00:40:14.292 --> 00:40:15.669
Look out.


00:40:16.947 --> 00:40:18.741
- Oh, my God.
- Be careful.


00:40:18.772 --> 00:40:20.148
Okay...


00:40:22.900 --> 00:40:24.564
What's going on
down there?


00:40:34.676 --> 00:40:35.956
Losberne Gallery.


00:40:35.988 --> 00:40:37.173
Special delivery.


00:40:37.204 --> 00:40:38.900
At this time of night?


00:40:38.932 --> 00:40:40.948
I'm right outside, mate.
Got a large package.


00:40:40.979 --> 00:40:43.571
Says, "artworks, fragile."


00:40:43.603 --> 00:40:45.876
I could leave it
on the doorstep if you want?


00:40:45.908 --> 00:40:47.476
No, no, no.
I'm coming. I'm coming.


00:40:47.508 --> 00:40:49.365
I was just in
the middle of something.


00:40:49.396 --> 00:40:50.516
One second.


00:40:51.027 --> 00:40:53.493
I'm at the window.
Where are you?


00:40:53.523 --> 00:40:55.572
<i>Um, let me
just check on that.</i>


00:40:55.604 --> 00:40:57.365
Sorry, mate. Wrong number.


00:41:07.923 --> 00:41:11.571
I wouldn't use that lav...
uh, bathroom for a bit.


00:41:12.404 --> 00:41:14.804
I'm sorry. You're going to have
to wait here for a moment.


00:41:14.836 --> 00:41:16.341
Brittles?


00:41:16.371 --> 00:41:17.812
Can you come up here, please?


00:41:26.133 --> 00:41:27.701
What is this?


00:41:31.668 --> 00:41:33.428
Search her bag.


00:41:33.972 --> 00:41:34.997
Hey!


00:41:35.667 --> 00:41:36.883
Excuse me!


00:41:41.684 --> 00:41:43.444
If that's the way
you treat all your interns,


00:41:43.475 --> 00:41:44.724
you can take
your work experience


00:41:44.755 --> 00:41:46.165
and shove it up your arse!


00:42:07.667 --> 00:42:09.300
Okay.


00:42:32.980 --> 00:42:36.052
<i>Our Dr. Losberne is gonna
get a surprise in the morning.</i>


00:42:36.083 --> 00:42:38.227
Until then,
you can take the night off.


00:42:38.260 --> 00:42:40.628
- Go out, have some fun.
- Yes!


00:42:40.660 --> 00:42:42.675
Yeah, but wait a minute.
Not too much fun


00:42:42.708 --> 00:42:45.076
because you're back
on duty at 7:00 a.m.


00:42:45.108 --> 00:42:46.163
7:00?


00:42:46.195 --> 00:42:48.019
We've all gotta be ready


00:42:48.052 --> 00:42:49.813
to move when
the phone goes.


00:42:49.843 --> 00:42:51.828
And I'll stay tuned to Losberne.


00:42:51.859 --> 00:42:55.028
Well, you know he might be
into some heavy phone sex,


00:42:55.060 --> 00:42:57.620
which means you might be in
for a steamy night, old boy.


00:42:57.651 --> 00:42:59.508
So there's this party.


00:42:59.540 --> 00:43:01.268
- What you saying?
- Red, you coming?


00:43:01.300 --> 00:43:02.740
She got plans.


00:43:06.900 --> 00:43:08.468
You did good.


00:43:21.331 --> 00:43:23.028
Mate, let's go.
Come on.


00:43:23.636 --> 00:43:24.981
Awkward.


00:43:39.540 --> 00:43:42.676
Come on, mate. Don't be such
a Debbie Downer.


00:43:42.707 --> 00:43:45.268
You know, there are
other birds in London.


00:43:45.748 --> 00:43:47.572
Come on.
Have a drink with us.


00:43:47.603 --> 00:43:49.940
No, I'm all right, mate.
Honestly.


00:43:49.971 --> 00:43:51.923
Come on.
You know you want to.


00:43:51.955 --> 00:43:53.204
Seriously, Batesy.


00:43:53.684 --> 00:43:55.061
I'm all right here.


00:43:55.923 --> 00:43:57.459
All right. Fine.


00:44:06.164 --> 00:44:07.733
- Hey.
- I said...


00:44:08.724 --> 00:44:11.028
Oi. You mug.


00:44:12.340 --> 00:44:13.812
She belongs to Sikes.


00:44:13.843 --> 00:44:15.700
You think
I don't know that?


00:44:15.731 --> 00:44:16.885
I don't belong to anyone.


00:44:24.691 --> 00:44:25.717
We'll see.


00:44:53.651 --> 00:44:56.084
Oi, Batesy!
Batesy, look out!


00:45:07.123 --> 00:45:09.172
I love coming here.


00:45:09.203 --> 00:45:11.092
You almost forget
you're in the city.


00:45:11.604 --> 00:45:13.684
How do you know
about this place?


00:45:13.715 --> 00:45:16.596
Uh, Sikes brought me
here once.


00:45:18.291 --> 00:45:19.700
Why'd you bring me
here then?


00:45:20.691 --> 00:45:23.796
Because I wanted to.
Is that okay?


00:45:24.979 --> 00:45:26.260
Hmm?


00:45:32.788 --> 00:45:34.548
Red!


00:45:46.036 --> 00:45:47.987
Seriously, why did
you bring me here?


00:45:48.019 --> 00:45:49.876
Why wouldn't
I bring you here?


00:45:49.907 --> 00:45:52.147
I don't think your girlfriend
would be too happy if she knew.


00:45:52.179 --> 00:45:54.132
Mmm, never said
she was my girlfriend.


00:45:55.635 --> 00:45:56.916
Why didn't you tell me?


00:45:57.652 --> 00:45:58.932
Tell you what?


00:46:00.052 --> 00:46:01.460
That you're only into...


00:46:01.491 --> 00:46:04.372
Girls?
Never said that either.


00:46:07.123 --> 00:46:08.467
I'm so confused.


00:46:22.547 --> 00:46:24.308
Oi! What the hell
are you doing?


00:46:35.956 --> 00:46:38.228
Hey. Don't tell anyone
about this, yeah?


00:46:38.964 --> 00:46:41.684
Red, if this is about Sikes,
you don't need to be scared.


00:46:41.716 --> 00:46:43.860
It's not me
I'm scared for.


00:47:01.204 --> 00:47:03.284
Got you!


00:47:03.315 --> 00:47:05.876
You think you're clever, don't you?
Call the police, love.


00:47:05.907 --> 00:47:08.244
- I will 'cause you're assaulting him!
- Assaulting him?


00:47:08.275 --> 00:47:11.059
- Yeah!
- This little bellend has been vandalizing property


00:47:11.092 --> 00:47:14.452
of the council with his
shitty little paintings.


00:47:14.483 --> 00:47:16.212
You wanna go as well, eh?


00:47:16.243 --> 00:47:17.523
Come on!


00:47:17.554 --> 00:47:19.667
Here they are.
Get down there, you! Go on.


00:47:19.700 --> 00:47:22.548
She's with the bellend there.
Arrest them.


00:47:22.579 --> 00:47:24.403
- Stay with them. It'll be okay.
- Come on, Son.


00:47:24.852 --> 00:47:26.100
I'll get Fagin.
Go on.


00:47:26.132 --> 00:47:27.828
Thank you.
All right.


00:47:35.764 --> 00:47:37.460
Personally I think
it's an improvement.


00:47:39.251 --> 00:47:40.405
So let me go.


00:47:41.171 --> 00:47:44.147
Unfortunately,
Metropolis Parking Solutions...


00:47:44.178 --> 00:47:46.291
That's the company
whose property you vandalized,


00:47:46.324 --> 00:47:49.109
they don't quite share
the same views.


00:47:54.356 --> 00:47:55.988
Little Ollie Twister.


00:48:01.906 --> 00:48:04.436
Look, to be honest, Oliver,
a little bit of graffiti


00:48:04.468 --> 00:48:06.740
is not really
what concerns me.


00:48:07.155 --> 00:48:09.171
You kind of running
into Warden Bumble,


00:48:09.204 --> 00:48:10.996
well that's just kind
of fortuitous for me.


00:48:11.028 --> 00:48:12.404
It's like
a happy accident.


00:48:13.139 --> 00:48:15.380
What I really wanna talk
to you about is...


00:48:18.995 --> 00:48:20.564
this man.


00:48:21.939 --> 00:48:22.964
Fagin.


00:48:23.794 --> 00:48:25.747
An alias, obviously.


00:48:25.779 --> 00:48:28.307
A once prestigious
art dealer.


00:48:28.339 --> 00:48:30.068
Then out of the blue...


00:48:30.099 --> 00:48:31.732
...vanishes.
Disappears.


00:48:32.403 --> 00:48:35.091
And since then, it seems
like he's been putting


00:48:35.124 --> 00:48:37.813
his knowledge of art
to more practical usage.


00:48:38.324 --> 00:48:41.045
Apparently he's running
quite the operation.


00:48:43.316 --> 00:48:44.629
Yeah.


00:48:45.715 --> 00:48:47.379
And what about
this lovely lady?


00:48:47.411 --> 00:48:48.916
Known associate of Fagin.


00:48:48.946 --> 00:48:50.292
Sikes.


00:48:51.763 --> 00:48:53.492
How am I supposed
to know these two?


00:48:55.314 --> 00:48:56.947
How am I supposed to...


00:48:58.547 --> 00:49:01.012
Nancy Lee, alias Red.


00:49:01.043 --> 00:49:03.955
Known associate of
both Sikes and Fagin's.


00:49:07.251 --> 00:49:08.947
It's a pretty girl,
Oliver.


00:49:14.931 --> 00:49:16.531
I can get you out of this,
you know.


00:49:17.299 --> 00:49:20.051
- Get me out of what?
- Ah, see, now that,


00:49:20.082 --> 00:49:22.387
that's exactly what I'm
hoping you're gonna tell me.


00:49:22.420 --> 00:49:24.052
Because your little friends,
your new pals,


00:49:24.084 --> 00:49:26.773
they're not all
that they seem.


00:49:27.252 --> 00:49:29.652
And to be perfectly honest,
friends of Fagin and Sikes


00:49:29.683 --> 00:49:31.572
have a nasty habit
of ending up, well...


00:49:35.059 --> 00:49:36.628
like that.


00:49:36.658 --> 00:49:38.931
Tom Chitling.
He died last month.


00:49:38.964 --> 00:49:41.332
Take a good look, Oliver.


00:49:41.363 --> 00:49:42.612
I don't even know this Sikes.


00:49:43.667 --> 00:49:45.332
Are you sure?


00:49:46.484 --> 00:49:47.989
I'm sure.


00:49:50.003 --> 00:49:51.029
Okay.


00:49:51.635 --> 00:49:53.715
Well,
you're free to go.


00:49:54.738 --> 00:49:58.003
Just be careful who you trust because
people only see what they wanna see.


00:50:00.467 --> 00:50:01.651
Off you go, then.


00:50:10.611 --> 00:50:11.956
You're late.


00:50:13.299 --> 00:50:14.803
Where's Twist?


00:50:15.891 --> 00:50:17.140
He was with you,
right, Dodge?


00:50:22.196 --> 00:50:24.596
Just wanted to get a run-in.
I lost track of time.


00:50:25.554 --> 00:50:26.868
I don't know
where Twist is.


00:50:26.899 --> 00:50:28.819
I gave them all the night off.


00:50:28.850 --> 00:50:31.571
Those paintings are going
nowhere till the morning.


00:50:31.604 --> 00:50:33.299
It is morning.
Where is he?


00:50:46.964 --> 00:50:48.756
- Who is this?
- <i>Think of me</i>


00:50:48.787 --> 00:50:50.803
<i>as the friendly uncle
you never had.</i>


00:50:50.835 --> 00:50:53.139
<i>I just wanted to make sure
you've got my number.</i>


00:50:53.780 --> 00:50:56.340
<i>In case you remember anything
about our Ms. Sikes.</i>


00:50:56.372 --> 00:50:57.621
I won't.


00:50:58.356 --> 00:51:00.500
You got some explaining
to do, boy.


00:51:02.355 --> 00:51:05.139
- Where you been, then?
- I went to a pub with Dodge and Batesy.


00:51:05.170 --> 00:51:07.603
They got back hours ago.
What happened to you?


00:51:08.595 --> 00:51:11.763
- I got arrested.
- Been having little words, have we?


00:51:11.795 --> 00:51:13.044
No, it wasn't
like that.


00:51:13.076 --> 00:51:14.708
It was this traffic warden.


00:51:14.739 --> 00:51:16.372
I wrote on his van
and he wasn't happy about it.


00:51:16.402 --> 00:51:18.196
You wrote
on his van last night?


00:51:18.227 --> 00:51:19.763
No, last week.


00:51:19.796 --> 00:51:21.459
I bumped into him
this morning...


00:51:21.491 --> 00:51:23.092
How come
the cops let you go?


00:51:23.891 --> 00:51:25.811
Did you give them
something they wanted?


00:51:25.843 --> 00:51:27.700
No, nothing.
I gave them nothing.


00:51:27.732 --> 00:51:29.108
If he grassed,
why would he come back here?


00:51:29.139 --> 00:51:30.292
Was I talking to you?


00:51:30.324 --> 00:51:32.180
- I'm just saying, I...
- Don't!


00:51:32.211 --> 00:51:34.483
- We need him.
- <i>Hello, Artnet.</i>


00:51:34.515 --> 00:51:36.595
- <i>Hello, it's Dr. Crispin Losberne.</i>
- Shh!


00:51:36.628 --> 00:51:38.643
<i>My vault is flooded, so I need
to move a painting to Dotheboy's.</i>


00:51:38.674 --> 00:51:40.371
He's on the phone
with the couriers.


00:51:40.402 --> 00:51:41.748
They're arranging a pickup.


00:51:41.779 --> 00:51:43.219
<i>One second.</i>


00:51:44.531 --> 00:51:46.195
Round three.


00:51:47.378 --> 00:51:49.107
The painting is gonna be
on the move.


00:51:49.138 --> 00:51:50.867
This is it.


00:51:50.898 --> 00:51:53.075
You better pray this time
it goes like clockwork.


00:51:55.732 --> 00:51:58.100
Remember,
I'm watching.


00:52:06.804 --> 00:52:08.948
I'm claustrophobic,
okay.


00:52:08.979 --> 00:52:11.412
Nobody told me that
it was gonna be that small.


00:52:11.827 --> 00:52:14.388
- Quit making a fuss and get in.
- I'm not making a fuss.


00:52:14.420 --> 00:52:17.138
I'm claustrophobic.
It's an actual condition.


00:52:17.171 --> 00:52:19.667
If Batesy gets in there
and passes out,


00:52:19.699 --> 00:52:21.556
the whole plan's screwed.
What are we gonna do?


00:52:21.587 --> 00:52:23.572
Exactly. And there is
every chance


00:52:23.603 --> 00:52:25.652
that if I get in there
I will pass out.


00:52:25.683 --> 00:52:27.476
Batesy,
don't be such a baby.


00:52:27.507 --> 00:52:29.523
What are you gonna do?
Force him down?


00:52:29.555 --> 00:52:31.635
You say you're gonna do
something then don't do it.


00:52:31.666 --> 00:52:34.964
Are we gonna do this,
or you gonna stand there arguing all day?


00:52:34.995 --> 00:52:36.084
Well, he's in now.


00:52:37.234 --> 00:52:40.372
All right. Anybody tries
to moves the crate,


00:52:40.404 --> 00:52:42.900
you set off the smoke bomb
in their face.


00:52:43.731 --> 00:52:44.915
Piece of cake.


00:52:45.586 --> 00:52:47.027
All right. That's it.


00:52:49.331 --> 00:52:50.323
Let's do it then.


00:52:53.618 --> 00:52:54.708
Really?


00:53:06.355 --> 00:53:08.563
Delivery to our gallery
in W1, yeah?


00:53:08.595 --> 00:53:09.875
Yeah, copy that, darling.


00:53:09.908 --> 00:53:11.348
We just got
a few drop-offs first.


00:53:11.380 --> 00:53:12.532
Cheers, lads.


00:53:36.435 --> 00:53:38.963
I thought we were only sharing travel
with the National Gallery piece.


00:53:38.995 --> 00:53:40.531
Uh, let me see.


00:53:40.562 --> 00:53:42.196
Originally yours
was dropped off first


00:53:42.227 --> 00:53:43.572
and then on
to the National Gallery.


00:53:43.603 --> 00:53:45.268
It's just an extra
pickup, mate.


00:53:45.298 --> 00:53:46.644
It won't affect
your drop-off time.


00:53:46.674 --> 00:53:49.042
They're close together,
you see.


00:53:49.074 --> 00:53:52.915
- Chiswell Fine Arts.
- I've never heard of it.


00:53:59.507 --> 00:54:01.907
You ever heard of
a Chiswell Fine Arts, Rosie?


00:54:01.939 --> 00:54:03.475
Somewhere near here?


00:54:03.890 --> 00:54:06.099
I thought you knew all
the galleries in London.


00:54:08.979 --> 00:54:10.963
I'll google it.


00:54:16.882 --> 00:54:19.284
Can't find a Chiswell.


00:54:22.003 --> 00:54:23.763
Get me Artnet
on the phone now!


00:54:45.011 --> 00:54:46.676
What's all this?


00:54:53.298 --> 00:54:54.579
You all right?
What's occurring?


00:54:54.610 --> 00:54:56.468
- Can we get through?
- How you doing?


00:54:56.498 --> 00:54:57.908
- Yeah, fine.
- Where you from?


00:54:57.939 --> 00:54:59.475
- I'm from Fullham.
- Fullham?


00:54:59.506 --> 00:55:02.291
I've got cousins in Fullham.
You know Phil?


00:55:02.323 --> 00:55:04.243
- No.
- You must know my second cousin.


00:55:04.275 --> 00:55:06.035
- What's her name? Oh, Tracey.
- No.


00:55:06.067 --> 00:55:07.859
- Can we get through?
- Can you get through?


00:55:07.891 --> 00:55:10.003
I don't know...


00:55:10.035 --> 00:55:12.596
<i>7-4, receiving. 7-4, receiving.</i>


00:55:12.626 --> 00:55:14.452
Is there aliens?
I mean...


00:55:14.482 --> 00:55:15.891
7-4. Go ahead.


00:55:15.923 --> 00:55:18.067
<i>Just had a call from
the Losberne Gallery.</i>


00:55:18.100 --> 00:55:20.339
<i>They seem to think
they're being robbed.</i>


00:55:20.371 --> 00:55:23.315
Is it real?
Is life even real?


00:55:23.347 --> 00:55:24.787
Everything all right,
lads?


00:55:25.875 --> 00:55:27.411
Floor it!


00:55:41.618 --> 00:55:43.219
No!


00:55:44.724 --> 00:55:46.867
Sikes, no.
No, Sikes!


00:55:47.411 --> 00:55:48.916
Please, Sikes.


00:55:51.891 --> 00:55:53.011
Run!


00:55:53.972 --> 00:55:56.819
- Where is it? Give it to me.
- I didn't get it. I'm sorry.


00:55:56.851 --> 00:55:59.891
We need a distraction.
Move. Move!


00:56:04.594 --> 00:56:06.642
When I said "don't,"
that means don't go this way.


00:56:06.675 --> 00:56:09.011
- <i>...female in a red leather jacket.</i>
- Hey!


00:56:09.042 --> 00:56:11.026
Female suspect heading west
down Pass Road.


00:56:11.059 --> 00:56:13.427
<i>Officers are in pursuit.
Officers are in pursuit.</i>


00:56:26.260 --> 00:56:27.828
I'm asking you
very nicely to stop.


00:56:31.475 --> 00:56:32.724
There it is.


00:56:57.138 --> 00:56:59.060
I really need
to start going to the gym.


00:56:59.955 --> 00:57:01.075
This is...


00:57:11.699 --> 00:57:12.948
Uh...


00:57:14.642 --> 00:57:16.370
<i>Bedwin, give me an update.</i>


00:57:16.402 --> 00:57:18.611
Brownlow, we got some good news
and some bad news.


00:57:18.643 --> 00:57:21.106
- <i>Fill me in then.</i>
- Yeah, well, the bad news is I haven't got her.


00:57:21.234 --> 00:57:24.275
- <i>What's the good news?</i>
- There is no good news, really, if I'm honest.


00:57:24.307 --> 00:57:26.003
<i>Get yourself back here now.</i>


00:57:32.947 --> 00:57:34.483
Oi! Get in.


00:57:35.284 --> 00:57:37.523
- I need to work on my cardio.
- How come Twist was


00:57:37.555 --> 00:57:39.284
in the back of that van?
Should have been you.


00:57:40.179 --> 00:57:43.443
Well, I'm claustrophobic,
so we just switched places.


00:57:45.940 --> 00:57:47.284
You shouldn't have.


00:57:54.227 --> 00:57:55.764
Batesy!


00:58:31.346 --> 00:58:33.074
He should have been
back by now.


00:58:33.106 --> 00:58:35.059
Quiet. I'm trying to think.


00:58:35.508 --> 00:58:37.715
That was our one shot.


00:58:39.154 --> 00:58:41.106
It was bad luck
is all.


00:58:41.555 --> 00:58:43.059
Bad luck? There's no such thing.


00:58:43.091 --> 00:58:45.747
It was a simple plan
until that bloody Twist


00:58:45.779 --> 00:58:47.954
decided to go in the van.


00:58:54.194 --> 00:58:56.052
Mate, have you seen...


00:58:58.323 --> 00:58:59.891
What happened
to Tom Chitling?


00:58:59.923 --> 00:59:01.011
He fell.


00:59:02.770 --> 00:59:06.610
- Did you see it?
- Someone has been misinforming you, Oliver.


00:59:06.643 --> 00:59:11.059
- Don't avoid the question!
- I just don't think it's you asking the questions.


00:59:11.091 --> 00:59:13.012
Who have you been talking to?


00:59:15.667 --> 00:59:17.172
Sikes.


00:59:17.778 --> 00:59:19.987
Why don't you ask her?


00:59:21.107 --> 00:59:22.899
- Sikes!
- He's a rat!


00:59:23.379 --> 00:59:25.427
Van suddenly peels off.
They knew what was going down.


00:59:25.459 --> 00:59:26.868
- I didn't tell them anything!
- Lies!


00:59:28.915 --> 00:59:30.259
What's this, eh?


00:59:32.883 --> 00:59:34.707
Thing I need to know, Twist,


00:59:34.739 --> 00:59:36.467
is how you hold up
under a beating.


00:59:37.011 --> 00:59:38.354
I bet you fall
to pieces, eh?


00:59:38.387 --> 00:59:39.603
Fagin, make her stop.


00:59:48.146 --> 00:59:49.874
Question is,
do you want some more?


00:59:52.659 --> 00:59:53.780
Hold him.


00:59:55.123 --> 00:59:57.202
Sikes, don't make it
permanent.


00:59:57.234 --> 00:59:58.963
Right, Bullseye,
on my command.


01:00:00.402 --> 01:00:02.354
You're making a mistake.


01:00:02.834 --> 01:00:04.243
A mistake?


01:00:05.106 --> 01:00:07.028
He got in trouble
with the traffic warden.


01:00:07.059 --> 01:00:08.916
And how would
you know that, Red?


01:00:09.554 --> 01:00:10.932
'Cause I was there.


01:00:12.050 --> 01:00:13.171
What?


01:00:15.411 --> 01:00:17.267
We were on our way home
and the traffic warden


01:00:17.299 --> 01:00:19.123
came out of nowhere
and tackled him to the ground.


01:00:19.155 --> 01:00:21.107
- Just like he said.
- On your way home from where?


01:00:23.698 --> 01:00:24.787
We...


01:00:26.003 --> 01:00:27.860
We went for a swim together.


01:00:40.851 --> 01:00:42.675
If he moves, shoot him.


01:00:42.707 --> 01:00:44.755
Come with me.


01:00:44.786 --> 01:00:46.003
Bullseye, stay.


01:00:58.675 --> 01:01:00.371
This ain't like Batesy.


01:01:00.402 --> 01:01:02.386
He gets withdrawal symptoms
if he ain't plugged in.


01:01:02.419 --> 01:01:04.723
- Batesy's dead.
- What?


01:01:04.754 --> 01:01:06.035
Just like she killed Tom.


01:01:06.610 --> 01:01:08.690
- But Sikes said...
- Tom was murdered!


01:01:09.426 --> 01:01:11.570
He didn't go off
that roof by accident.


01:01:12.851 --> 01:01:14.259
How would you know that?


01:01:15.411 --> 01:01:16.660
I got a text
off that phone.


01:01:18.226 --> 01:01:19.762
Some cop gave it to me
to see if I'd turn.


01:01:19.795 --> 01:01:21.523
And did you turn?


01:01:21.555 --> 01:01:24.500
Or were you never
with this family to begin with?


01:01:25.010 --> 01:01:26.675
You call this a family?


01:01:27.379 --> 01:01:28.946
When that psycho is
out there with Red


01:01:28.979 --> 01:01:30.579
and you're pointing
a gun at me!


01:01:31.731 --> 01:01:32.947
I don't believe you.


01:01:32.978 --> 01:01:34.514
I'm gonna go find Batesy myself.


01:01:34.547 --> 01:01:36.052
You're gonna be looking
six feet under.


01:01:36.499 --> 01:01:39.283
He's right. I pushed Tom.


01:01:39.314 --> 01:01:41.170
- You lying piece...
- Please.


01:01:41.202 --> 01:01:42.995
Give me an excuse to kill you.


01:01:43.411 --> 01:01:44.627
You can't kill all of us.


01:01:45.394 --> 01:01:46.579
Let's see, shall we?


01:01:47.155 --> 01:01:49.363
Six bullets, three kids.
You do the math.


01:01:49.395 --> 01:01:51.731
We're hitting Dotheboy's.
We're getting that painting.


01:01:51.763 --> 01:01:53.619
Dotheboy's?
I think the whole plan


01:01:53.650 --> 01:01:56.146
was to get the painting
before it went there.


01:01:56.178 --> 01:01:58.387
That place
is impenetrable.


01:01:58.419 --> 01:02:00.019
You scared, old man?


01:02:00.530 --> 01:02:02.931
I'll have a plan
in four hours.


01:02:03.442 --> 01:02:06.483
Try not to kill any more
of them in the meantime.


01:02:09.138 --> 01:02:10.451
I can't promise anything.


01:02:18.898 --> 01:02:21.010
<i>Look, mate,
I believe ya.</i>


01:02:21.683 --> 01:02:24.019
<i>What Sikes did to Tom,
that's messed up.</i>


01:02:24.594 --> 01:02:26.899
But if we don't do this,
we'll lose Red too.


01:02:28.403 --> 01:02:30.163
Sikes is a loose cannon.


01:02:30.194 --> 01:02:32.243
Let's just suck it up
and get on with it, yeah?


01:02:33.938 --> 01:02:35.283
Let's do this.


01:02:41.970 --> 01:02:43.058
<i>Is he on time?</i>


01:02:43.090 --> 01:02:45.780
Like clockwork. We're on.


01:02:58.227 --> 01:02:59.891
Can I get two sugars
with that, as well?


01:03:00.626 --> 01:03:02.354
All right there, mates?
Sorry to interrupt.


01:03:02.386 --> 01:03:04.210
Can I get a Bakewell tart,
please?


01:03:04.242 --> 01:03:05.747
Sure.


01:03:06.259 --> 01:03:08.083
- It's chippy, innit?
- Yeah, I know. It's freezing.


01:03:08.115 --> 01:03:09.843
There you go. 1.50.


01:03:10.292 --> 01:03:11.634
There you go.
Keep the change.


01:03:12.882 --> 01:03:13.972
Thanks.


01:03:16.211 --> 01:03:17.522
Have a good day,
lads.


01:03:17.554 --> 01:03:18.739
See ya.


01:03:33.074 --> 01:03:36.530
<i>The painting will be under
lock and key before the auction.</i>


01:03:36.946 --> 01:03:39.891
<i>So our only chance is
during the main event.</i>


01:03:39.922 --> 01:03:42.610
<i>We'll go in at the front
and at the right moment</i>


01:03:42.643 --> 01:03:45.523
<i>execute the plan,
sending the painting your way.</i>


01:03:45.554 --> 01:03:47.571
Let's play happy families, eh?
Big smiles.


01:04:05.459 --> 01:04:07.123
Thank you.


01:04:07.154 --> 01:04:09.074
Whoa, whoa.


01:04:09.106 --> 01:04:11.123
It's the chair. Really?


01:04:11.635 --> 01:04:12.819
Jesus.


01:04:29.426 --> 01:04:31.442
There you go.


01:04:31.474 --> 01:04:34.099
<i>Dodge, once you're
inside, let Twist in.</i>


01:04:34.131 --> 01:04:36.210
<i>Then, when all hell
has broken loose,</i>


01:04:36.242 --> 01:04:37.362
<i>you know what to do.</i>


01:04:42.803 --> 01:04:44.051
Gang's all here.


01:04:52.530 --> 01:04:54.323
Don't do anything stupid.


01:05:03.283 --> 01:05:06.130
I'm glad you're finally taking
this threat seriously, Officer.


01:05:07.794 --> 01:05:09.396
Detective Inspector.


01:05:15.762 --> 01:05:17.172
How many men
have you deployed?


01:05:18.291 --> 01:05:19.635
There's 12
inside the building.


01:05:20.466 --> 01:05:22.163
Another 20 outside.


01:05:25.810 --> 01:05:27.315
Nobody is getting
this painting, Losberne.


01:05:27.346 --> 01:05:28.979
Doctor Losberne.


01:05:38.962 --> 01:05:40.594
Better you than me,
mate.


01:05:56.818 --> 01:05:58.387
<i>Lot 146.</i>


01:05:59.123 --> 01:06:00.914
William Hogarth's painting


01:06:00.946 --> 01:06:03.635
<i>A Harlot's Progress,
The Arrest.</i>


01:06:03.666 --> 01:06:06.546
Oil on canvas. 1731.


01:06:06.578 --> 01:06:08.658
Has resurfaced
after many years,


01:06:08.690 --> 01:06:11.442
as the only surviving <i>Harlot's
Progress</i> from the fire...


01:06:11.474 --> 01:06:12.979
Now.


01:06:13.555 --> 01:06:17.139
We start the reserve
price of three million pounds.


01:06:17.169 --> 01:06:18.642
Yes, madam.


01:06:20.018 --> 01:06:22.770
And you, sir? At the back there, sir? Yes.


01:06:22.803 --> 01:06:24.403
Three million two.


01:06:24.435 --> 01:06:25.971
I have three million,
200 thousand pounds.


01:06:28.241 --> 01:06:29.747
He's got a gun!


01:06:31.699 --> 01:06:33.619
- Stay calm.
- It was a trap.


01:06:33.649 --> 01:06:36.338
- They're after my painting!
- Get it back in the vault!


01:06:36.370 --> 01:06:38.035
It'll be safe.
It's the safest place.


01:06:43.315 --> 01:06:45.714
- Over there, look.
- Through that door.


01:06:50.482 --> 01:06:53.203
There's a robbery in progress.
Stay with the painting.


01:06:53.235 --> 01:06:55.091
Get it to the vault.
Let's go! Let's move.


01:06:58.322 --> 01:07:00.242
Wait, wait, wait.


01:07:00.274 --> 01:07:01.939
I'm coming with you.


01:07:01.970 --> 01:07:03.283
No one goes
down there but us.


01:07:03.314 --> 01:07:05.075
There's a robbery in progress.


01:07:05.107 --> 01:07:07.986
- Yeah, we have our procedures.
- And I have my orders.


01:07:08.019 --> 01:07:10.771
And that painting ain't going
anywhere without me.


01:07:10.803 --> 01:07:12.755
What... What's going on?


01:07:12.786 --> 01:07:15.571
- Who are you?
- Officer Dawkins, Sergeant.


01:07:15.602 --> 01:07:17.362
- Dawkins? Good.
- Yeah.


01:07:59.123 --> 01:08:01.907
Okay. You guys go that way.
You guys come with me. Let's go.


01:08:08.146 --> 01:08:09.330
You.


01:08:10.002 --> 01:08:12.371
Yes, it's me.


01:08:14.001 --> 01:08:15.954
Ah, that felt good.


01:08:31.570 --> 01:08:33.619
Good. This is good.
This is very good.


01:08:34.642 --> 01:08:36.148
Whoa, whoa, whoa.


01:08:39.410 --> 01:08:40.596
Show me the painting.


01:08:42.193 --> 01:08:43.186
Ah...


01:08:45.042 --> 01:08:46.898
I'll be honest,
not his best work.


01:08:50.738 --> 01:08:52.147
Move!


01:08:52.178 --> 01:08:53.171
Okay.


01:08:57.266 --> 01:08:59.090
Oh, you silly sausage.


01:08:59.122 --> 01:09:00.403
You're going nowhere, Son.


01:09:02.257 --> 01:09:03.763
Shit!


01:09:05.715 --> 01:09:07.730
Brownlow,
you're wrong about Twist.


01:09:07.762 --> 01:09:09.203
He's in the lift shaft.


01:09:09.234 --> 01:09:10.962
Yeah, the dirty swine.


01:09:12.466 --> 01:09:13.940
Well, move then.


01:09:17.618 --> 01:09:19.634
I'm coming for you, Twist.


01:09:19.665 --> 01:09:22.579
- No, no, no!
- If you think a lift is gonna stop me...


01:09:23.475 --> 01:09:26.291
- Oh, you got nowhere to hide, boy.
- Dodge!


01:09:26.323 --> 01:09:27.379
- You muppet.
- Dodge?


01:09:27.410 --> 01:09:29.234
You...


01:09:29.265 --> 01:09:30.322
Hurry up.


01:09:30.354 --> 01:09:31.538
- Dodge.
- Come on.


01:09:31.570 --> 01:09:32.818
Help me!


01:09:32.851 --> 01:09:34.739
- Hurry up.
- Help!


01:09:34.770 --> 01:09:36.755
- Come on.
- I'm coming!


01:09:36.787 --> 01:09:38.419
Get these bloody doors open!


01:09:47.858 --> 01:09:49.107
Hurry up, Dodge!


01:10:02.641 --> 01:10:04.146
Oi!


01:10:10.545 --> 01:10:12.081
Wait a minute.


01:10:12.113 --> 01:10:14.066
Give me a break.
You're not thinking we...


01:10:14.098 --> 01:10:16.275
- Oi! Stop!
- Come on!


01:10:18.898 --> 01:10:21.459
- Ready? Belt.
- Twist, what are you doing? This is madness.


01:10:21.489 --> 01:10:23.058
Three, two, one...


01:10:26.354 --> 01:10:27.538
Hang on!


01:10:28.338 --> 01:10:29.843
Wait, wait...


01:10:29.874 --> 01:10:31.058
Let go!


01:10:37.010 --> 01:10:38.802
Okay.


01:10:38.834 --> 01:10:40.082
Congratulations.


01:10:41.107 --> 01:10:42.227
All the best.


01:10:45.938 --> 01:10:47.827
Brownlow, you need
to get down here right now.


01:10:53.265 --> 01:10:54.514
Shit!


01:10:54.546 --> 01:10:57.906
Shit, shit!


01:10:57.938 --> 01:11:00.018
- Flippin' hell.
- Let's go up here.


01:11:01.937 --> 01:11:03.699
I think we've lost them.


01:11:03.729 --> 01:11:05.779
They wouldn't have got far,
Losberne.


01:11:05.810 --> 01:11:07.154
Well,
you better be right.


01:11:07.794 --> 01:11:09.586
- Come on. Let's go.
- Hey! Hey!


01:11:09.617 --> 01:11:11.123
Don't even think about it!
Do not move.


01:11:11.153 --> 01:11:13.425
Hello?


01:11:13.457 --> 01:11:15.506
- <i>Your delivery's here.</i>
- I didn't order anything.


01:11:16.243 --> 01:11:18.643
- Hey, don't!
- Dodge, let's go!


01:11:19.634 --> 01:11:21.106
Hey!


01:11:21.138 --> 01:11:23.155
Get after them!
Don't leave, hey!


01:11:23.185 --> 01:11:25.235
- Come back here! Come...
- Wait!


01:11:25.266 --> 01:11:28.274
Get them... Hey, stop!


01:11:28.305 --> 01:11:30.866
Stop! Make him stop!


01:11:48.307 --> 01:11:51.091
There's only one person
who could do this.


01:11:57.170 --> 01:11:58.706
<i>Batesy.</i>


01:11:58.737 --> 01:12:00.050
Enjoy your munch, did ya?


01:12:00.082 --> 01:12:02.578
You magnificent bastard.


01:12:02.611 --> 01:12:06.482
You had us worried sick, mate.
Where are ya?


01:12:06.513 --> 01:12:09.330
You know Sikes has gone
full-blown psycho, don't you?


01:12:09.362 --> 01:12:11.025
- <i>She tried to kill me.</i>
- What?


01:12:11.058 --> 01:12:12.531
We're on our way
to see her now.


01:12:12.562 --> 01:12:14.386
<i>No, don't! It ain't safe.</i>


01:12:14.418 --> 01:12:16.915
What do you mean?
We got no choice.


01:12:16.946 --> 01:12:19.091
<i>Red's with her.
We're all heading to Fagin's.</i>


01:12:20.243 --> 01:12:21.875
All right, well,
I'll meet you there.


01:12:21.907 --> 01:12:23.411
- <i>Just look after yourself.</i>
- Okay.


01:12:24.593 --> 01:12:26.642
That was Batesy. He's...


01:12:29.234 --> 01:12:30.418
Twist?


01:12:34.898 --> 01:12:36.114
Twist?


01:12:39.857 --> 01:12:41.683
You're late.
Where is he?


01:12:42.257 --> 01:12:43.986
I don't know.
We got split up.


01:12:44.017 --> 01:12:45.585
- Who's got it?
- He has.


01:12:45.618 --> 01:12:46.835
Oi!


01:12:47.762 --> 01:12:49.906
- You miss me?
- Bates.


01:12:50.482 --> 01:12:52.306
You all right?
What happened?


01:12:52.337 --> 01:12:54.451
Thought I dealt with you,
fuck's sake.


01:12:54.481 --> 01:12:56.561
- Where's Twist?
- I'm right here.


01:13:04.402 --> 01:13:06.258
You want the painting?
She's coming with me.


01:13:07.539 --> 01:13:08.979
Do you think she's worth it?


01:13:12.721 --> 01:13:13.714
Try me.


01:13:15.250 --> 01:13:16.851
Do what he says.


01:13:21.458 --> 01:13:23.539
You got more stones than
I gave you credit for.


01:13:25.329 --> 01:13:26.835
Give me that.


01:13:32.689 --> 01:13:34.642
I'll always be
a step ahead of you.


01:13:38.033 --> 01:13:39.890
You think
you can just take my girl?


01:13:41.265 --> 01:13:42.290
It's the painting, Sikes.


01:13:42.737 --> 01:13:44.946
Give me the envelope
and let him go.


01:13:46.034 --> 01:13:47.154
You sure that's it, Fagin?


01:13:52.050 --> 01:13:53.971
- What?
- The painting.


01:13:54.641 --> 01:13:56.018
Are you sure
it's the right one?


01:14:00.722 --> 01:14:02.611
Easy. Easy.


01:14:03.185 --> 01:14:04.850
I'm just reaching for my phone.


01:14:05.425 --> 01:14:07.346
You guys might wanna see this.


01:14:13.298 --> 01:14:15.155
You see,
before I got into graffiti,


01:14:15.922 --> 01:14:17.587
I used to paint.


01:14:17.618 --> 01:14:20.881
You lot mentioning Hogarth
got me inspired.


01:14:20.914 --> 01:14:22.739
It's not bad, eh, Fagin?


01:14:23.505 --> 01:14:24.690
Where is it?


01:14:25.073 --> 01:14:26.771
I walk out of here
with Red.


01:14:27.505 --> 01:14:29.298
I'll call you
and tell you where it is.


01:14:29.329 --> 01:14:30.675
She stays with me.


01:14:32.081 --> 01:14:33.682
We need the painting, Sikes.


01:14:33.713 --> 01:14:35.570
Whose side are you on?


01:14:35.602 --> 01:14:38.707
All this has got to stop.
You're done. We're done.


01:14:38.739 --> 01:14:40.723
All bets are off.


01:14:40.754 --> 01:14:43.826
Get me the envelope
and I'll let you leave.


01:14:57.298 --> 01:14:58.481
Come on.


01:14:59.378 --> 01:15:00.913
You'll let me leave?


01:15:07.154 --> 01:15:08.850
I choose how this ends.


01:15:09.873 --> 01:15:11.507
- Fagin, Fagin.
- Fagin.


01:15:12.018 --> 01:15:13.011
Fagin?


01:15:19.090 --> 01:15:20.466
Come on!


01:15:21.202 --> 01:15:23.346
Quick! Come on, Twist!


01:15:35.857 --> 01:15:37.266
Come on!


01:15:41.778 --> 01:15:43.219
You go first.


01:15:43.250 --> 01:15:44.691
I'm not going without you!


01:15:44.722 --> 01:15:46.963
Listen, jump.
I'll be right behind you.


01:15:47.473 --> 01:15:48.466
Go.


01:16:05.553 --> 01:16:07.345
Twist! Twist.


01:16:07.377 --> 01:16:08.626
Hold on, hold on.


01:16:08.657 --> 01:16:10.227
Come on!


01:16:14.994 --> 01:16:17.298
Twist! Come on.


01:16:17.330 --> 01:16:18.674
Don't let go.


01:16:26.289 --> 01:16:28.274
No! No!


01:16:31.219 --> 01:16:34.355
- Pull him up, Sikes.
- I'm sure he'll be fine. Step back!


01:16:34.385 --> 01:16:36.465
Look at him, not even strong
enough to pull himself up.


01:16:36.498 --> 01:16:39.026
- He's so weak.
- He's not weak!


01:16:39.058 --> 01:16:41.842
- You need to come with me now.
- I don't need you anymore.


01:16:41.873 --> 01:16:43.602
You think Twist is
the one for you?


01:16:43.633 --> 01:16:45.011
He's more than
you will ever be.


01:16:45.041 --> 01:16:46.739
I dragged you from the gutter,
looked after you,


01:16:46.770 --> 01:16:48.530
gave you everything
you needed.


01:16:48.561 --> 01:16:49.810
Sikes!


01:17:06.610 --> 01:17:09.843
What a fine thing
capital punishment is.


01:17:42.578 --> 01:17:44.051
Young man.


01:17:47.281 --> 01:17:49.202
I'm guessing you heard
about the reward?


01:17:53.265 --> 01:17:54.867
Be there in five.


01:17:59.889 --> 01:18:02.289
Do we know what we're meant
to be waiting for?


01:18:02.321 --> 01:18:04.499
We don't have a clue,
Bedwin.


01:18:04.529 --> 01:18:06.515
I'm sure we'll know
when we see it.


01:18:06.546 --> 01:18:08.691
He's not exactly just gonna stroll in.


01:18:08.721 --> 01:18:11.250
- He's literally just strolled in.
- All right, lads?


01:18:11.761 --> 01:18:14.161
- You hungry?
- You got a lot of nerve showing up.


01:18:14.193 --> 01:18:16.306
- Let's just nick him now.
- Calm down, Bedwin.


01:18:16.338 --> 01:18:18.002
You look like you could do
with a bacon sarnie.


01:18:18.034 --> 01:18:19.762
This might be funny to you,
but this is serious.


01:18:19.792 --> 01:18:21.009
I need your full cooperation.


01:18:21.042 --> 01:18:23.059
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Cooperation?


01:18:23.666 --> 01:18:25.235
I've done you guys a favor.


01:18:26.001 --> 01:18:27.634
How's that?


01:18:27.666 --> 01:18:28.754
Where's the painting?


01:18:28.784 --> 01:18:30.067
I don't have it.


01:18:30.098 --> 01:18:31.602
So where is it?


01:18:31.634 --> 01:18:33.361
I'm not the criminal here.
In fact,


01:18:33.394 --> 01:18:34.898
I've done all the work
for you guys.


01:18:34.929 --> 01:18:36.786
Two bacon sarnies.


01:18:36.817 --> 01:18:38.066
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


01:18:38.097 --> 01:18:39.730
Excuse me. I didn't order this.


01:18:39.762 --> 01:18:42.035
Oh, no, it's fine.
It's my treat.


01:18:42.065 --> 01:18:44.177
Well, that's very kind of you,
young man.


01:18:44.210 --> 01:18:47.378
- Yes, very kind.
- But don't think this is getting you out of trouble.


01:18:47.409 --> 01:18:48.722
I need you to understand
one thing.


01:18:48.753 --> 01:18:50.513
You're gonna need
to start cooperating.


01:18:53.809 --> 01:18:55.217
Oh, brilliant.


01:19:05.330 --> 01:19:07.282
Yeah, hello?
Very smart that was.


01:19:07.313 --> 01:19:08.977
<i>A wise cop
once said to me,</i>


01:19:09.008 --> 01:19:10.929
<i>"People only see
what they wanna see."</i>


01:19:10.961 --> 01:19:13.777
<i>You'll be wanting some
brown sauce with those I assume.</i>


01:19:13.808 --> 01:19:16.466
What do you mean... Hello? Hello?


01:19:19.217 --> 01:19:20.529
Brown sauce.


01:19:23.633 --> 01:19:24.913
Nah, it's...


01:19:28.433 --> 01:19:29.969
It's above
the brown sauce, Bedwin.


01:19:30.001 --> 01:19:31.507
It's above
the brown sauce.


01:19:33.553 --> 01:19:35.090
Holy shit.


01:19:49.297 --> 01:19:52.818
<i>The tale of the stolen Hogarth
in an audacious raid</i>


01:19:52.850 --> 01:19:54.802
<i>took a bizarre twist today</i>


01:19:54.832 --> 01:19:58.130
<i>when a tip-off led detectives
to a lockup in East London</i>


01:19:58.162 --> 01:20:01.970
<i>in which a large collection of
stolen artworks has been discovered.</i>


01:20:02.002 --> 01:20:06.131
<i>The lockup belongs to the art
dealer Dr. Crispin Losberne.</i>


01:20:06.705 --> 01:20:10.386
<i>Documents were also found
proving that Dr. Crispin Losberne</i>


01:20:10.417 --> 01:20:13.330
<i>is not the legal owner
of the Hogarth.</i>


01:20:13.362 --> 01:20:16.306
<i>It's alleged that
the well-established art dealer</i>


01:20:16.338 --> 01:20:19.859
<i>has been making his fortune
out of selling stolen artwork</i>


01:20:19.890 --> 01:20:22.482
<i>and faking
the ownership documentation.</i>


01:20:22.514 --> 01:20:25.906
<i>A Mr. Isaac Solomon
has been named as an accomplice.</i>


01:20:25.937 --> 01:20:29.459
<i>It's believed that this man
also goes by the name of Fagin.</i>


01:20:30.065 --> 01:20:32.658
<i>Fagin and Sikes really
had raised some good thieves.</i>


01:20:32.689 --> 01:20:35.505
<i>So good they didn't know
when they were the target.</i>


01:20:40.338 --> 01:20:42.866
<i>The envelope revealed
the true owners of the Hogarth</i>


01:20:42.897 --> 01:20:46.098
<i>and the key to the lockup where
Losberne kept the stolen paintings.</i>


01:20:56.433 --> 01:21:00.082
- Holy shit.
- <i>Even Bedwin and Brownlow deserved a break.</i>


01:21:00.112 --> 01:21:02.226
<i>In other arts-related news,</i>


01:21:02.257 --> 01:21:05.745
<i>a mystery painting arrived
with a special delivery</i>


01:21:05.776 --> 01:21:08.913
<i>for a new exhibition at
the National Gallery last week.</i>


01:21:08.945 --> 01:21:12.626
<i>The question everyone's asking
is: How did it get there?</i>


01:21:13.266 --> 01:21:16.369
<i>The painting was added
to the exhibition by mistake</i>


01:21:16.402 --> 01:21:19.538
<i>but critics have gone wild
for this unknown artist</i>


01:21:19.569 --> 01:21:22.290
<i>and have demanded
the piece remains on display.</i>


01:21:27.474 --> 01:21:28.914
There you go, Mum.


01:21:32.817 --> 01:21:36.753
<i>In fact, people can't stop
talking about the mystery artist,</i>


01:21:36.786 --> 01:21:39.506
<i>with many asking
who is Molly Twist</i>


01:21:39.537 --> 01:21:42.578
<i>and when and where
will all of her work appear.</i>


01:21:42.608 --> 01:21:45.969
<i>Dealers are said to be willing
to offer up to 50,000</i>


01:21:46.000 --> 01:21:49.009
<i>to anyone with
an original Twist painting.</i>


01:22:06.512 --> 01:22:08.113
Cheers, Nancy.


01:22:10.129 --> 01:22:12.977
Call me that again, Oliver,
and I will twist something you don't like.


01:22:15.249 --> 01:22:17.298
All right, quit canoodling.


01:22:19.952 --> 01:22:23.058
So, are you gonna stick
with us, kid?


01:22:23.089 --> 01:22:24.882
Come on,
you know you wanna.


01:22:24.914 --> 01:22:27.314
Look, if I'm gonna be
staying around,


01:22:27.345 --> 01:22:29.361
we gotta cut out all
the nonsense and go straight.


01:22:29.392 --> 01:22:32.561
- Whoa, wait.
- He's joking, right? That must be a joke.


01:22:32.593 --> 01:22:36.050
What exactly do you expect
us lot to do for a job, eh?


01:22:36.753 --> 01:22:38.706
You ever thought about
selling paintings?


01:22:39.666 --> 01:22:42.066
A bag full of Molly Twist art
is worth a few quid.


01:22:43.601 --> 01:22:44.594
Hmm?


01:22:45.393 --> 01:22:48.689
<i>Like I said, no singing,
no dancing.</i>


01:22:48.722 --> 01:22:50.802
<i>But maybe I was wrong about
the happy ending.</i>


01:22:51.762 --> 01:22:54.514
<i>I know these people.
I belong with them.</i>


01:25:42.482 --> 01:25:45.107
